{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Now I have a clear picture. The main costs for the largest case (~125 ms total):\n\n1. **Projections (q,k,v)**: ~41 ms (33%) — three GEMMs at ~13.5 ms each\n2. **Softmax (p0 + p1)**: ~33 ms (26%) — p1 softmax is bigger due to irregular logits\n3. **p@G (norm computation)**: ~25 ms (20%) — two matmuls at ~12.5 ms each\n4. **p1 logits**: ~5 ms (4%)\n5. **p_mix @ v**: ~3 ms (2%)\n6. **G computation**: ~3 ms (2%)\n7. **Other**: ~13 ms (10%)\n\nLet me think about what can be optimized:\n\n**Projections**: Each GEMM is (B*L, C) @ (C, H*D) = (B*L, H*D). For B=1, L=256, C=1280, H*D=1280: 256×1280 @ 1280×1280. These are small GEMMs where overhead matters. Fusing into one big GEMM might help.\n\n**Softmax**: This is surprising — two softmaxes of (B,H,L,L) = (1,20,256,256) = 1.3M elements take 33ms? That seems slow. Let me check if there's a way to speed this up.\n\n**p@G norms**: Two L×L matmuls per head × H heads. Could potentially be optimized.\n\nLet me try a few more ideas:\n1. **Fused QKV projection** into one big GEMM\n2. **Optimizing softmax** by reshaping to 2D\n3. **Combining p@G computations** — since we need both p1@G and p_mix@G\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat << 'PYEOF' > /tmp/profile8.py\nimport math\nimport time\nimport torch\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nalpha, beta = 1.05, 7.5\n\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C)\nwq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n\ninv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\nxr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\nwq_r = wq.reshape(H*D, C)\nwk_r = wk.reshape(H*D, C)\nwv_r = wv.reshape(H*D, C)\n\ndef bench(name, fn, n=30):\n    for _ in range(3): fn()\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        fn()\n        times.append(time.perf_counter() - t0)\n    times.sort()\n    med = times[n//2] * 1000\n    print(f\\\"  {name:45s}: {med:7.3f} ms\\\")\n    return med\n\n# === Fused QKV projection ===\nprint(\\\"=== Fused QKV projection ===\\\")\nw_qkv = torch.cat([wq_r, wk_r, wv_r], dim=0)  # (3*H*D, C) = (3840, 1280)\nprint(f\\\"  w_qkv shape: {w_qkv.shape}\\\")\n\ndef fused_qkv_permute():\n    out = xr @ w_qkv.T  # (B*L, 3*H*D) = (256, 3840)\n    out = out.reshape(B, L, 3, H, D).permute(2, 0, 3, 1, 4)\n    return out[0], out[1], out[2]\n\ndef fused_qkv_separate():\n    out = xr @ w_qkv.T  # (256, 3840)\n    out = out.reshape(B, L, 3, H, D)\n    q = out[:, :, 0, :, :].permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = out[:, :, 1, :, :].permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = out[:, :, 2, :, :].permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    return q, k, v\n\ndef three_separate():\n    q = (xr @ wq_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    k = (xr @ wk_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    v = (xr @ wv_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    return q, k, v\n\nbench(\\\"3 separate projections\\\", three_separate)\nbench(\\\"fused qkv + permute\\\", fused_qkv_permute)\nbench(\\\"fused qkv + separate contig\\\", fused_qkv_separate)\n\nq, k, v = three_separate()\nqf, kf, vf = fused_qkv_separate()\nprint(f\\\"  q diff: {(q-qf).abs().max():.2e}\\\")\n\n# === Softmax optimization ===\nprint(\\\"\\\\n=== Softmax optimization ===\\\")\nlogits = torch.randn(B, H, L, L) * 0.5\n\nbench(\\\"softmax dim=-1 (B,H,L,L)\\\", lambda: logits.softmax(dim=-1))\nbench(\\\"softmax dim=-1 contiguous first\\\", lambda: logits.contiguous().softmax(dim=-1))\nbench(\\\"softmax on reshape (B*H*L, L)\\\", lambda: logits.reshape(B*H*L, L).softmax(dim=-1).reshape(B, H, L, L))\nbench(\\\"softmax on (B*H, L*L) no, wrong dim...\\\", lambda: logits.reshape(B*H, L*L))  # just reshape timing\n\n# Try in-place softmax?\ndef inplace_softmax():\n    x = logits.clone()\n    x.softmax_(dim=-1)\n    return x\nbench(\\\"in-place softmax (with clone)\\\", inplace_softmax)\n\n# Check: does the output need to be contiguous?\nsm = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\nprint(f\\\"  softmax output contiguous: {sm.is_contiguous()}\\\")\n\n# === Norm computation: can we share work between p1 and p_mix? ===\nprint(\\\"\\\\n=== Norm computation sharing ===\\\")\np0 = torch.randn(B, H, L, L).softmax(dim=-1)\np1 = torch.randn(B, H, L, L).softmax(dim=-1)\np_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\nG = (xr @ xr.T).reshape(B, L, L)\nG_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n# Current: compute p1@G and p_mix@G separately\n# Alternative: compute p0@G + p1@G, then p_mix@G = lerp(p0@G, p1@G, beta)\n# Cost: same number of matmuls (2), but potentially less memory pressure?\n\n# But wait, do we need p0@G? We need norm0_sq = (p0@G * p0).sum\n# And cross term: (p0@G * p1).sum = p0 @ G @ p1\"'^T diagonal\n# normm_sq = (1-beta)''^2 * norm0 + beta''^2 * norm1 + 2*(1-beta)*beta * cross\n# This avoids computing p_mix @ G entirely!\n# But we need p0@G (for norm0 and cross) and we already have p1@G (for norm1)\n# Cost: p0@G + p1@G = 2 matmuls (same as before: p1@G + p_mix@G)\n# But p_mix computation is cheaper (lerp is BHL², matmul is BH L³)\n# Wait, no. We still need p_mix for p_mix @ v.\n# But we save the p_mix @ G matmul and add a p0 @ G matmul instead. Same count.\n\n# Hmm, but there might be cache benefits. Let'\"'s check.\n\ndef norm_current():\n    p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n    pmG = p_mix @ G_exp\n    n1 = (p1G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n    nm = (pmG * p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True).sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n    return n1 / nm\n\ndef norm_shared():\n    p0G = p0 @ G_exp\n    p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n    n0_sq = (p0G * p0).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n    n1_sq = (p1G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n    cross = (p0G * p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)  # = (p1G * p0).sum\n    b0 = 1.0 - beta\n    nm_sq = b0*b0 * n0_sq + beta*beta * n1_sq + 2*b0*beta * cross\n    n1 = n1_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n    nm = nm_sq.sqrt().clamp_min(1e-6)\n    return n1 / nm\n\nbench(\\\"norm current (p1@G + pmix@G)\\\", norm_current)\nbench(\\\"norm shared (p0@G + p1@G + formula)\\\", norm_shared)\n\nr_curr = norm_current()\nr_sh = norm_shared()\nprint(f\\\"  norm diff: {(r_curr-r_sh).abs().max():.2e}\\\")\n\n# === Can we compute softmax of p1 more efficiently? ===\n# p1 = softmax(a_p * A + a_m * A\"'^T)\n# A = q @ k''^T * s, so A''^T = k @ q''^T * s\n# a_p * A + a_m * A''^T = a_p * qk''^T + a_m * kq''^T (scaled)\n# Can we compute this without materializing A?\n# For softmax, we need the full matrix anyway for the max subtraction.\n\nprint(\"'\"\\\\n=== p1 logits: different computation orders ===\\\")\nq = (xr @ wq_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\nk = (xr @ wk_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\nA = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2) * inv_sqrt_d\n\na_p = 0.5 * (1 + alpha)\na_m = 0.5 * (1 - alpha)\n\n# Current: a_p * A + a_m * A\"'^T\nbench(\"a_p * A + a_m * A''^T\", lambda: a_p * A + a_m * A.transpose(-1, -2))\n\n# Alternative: a_p * qk''^T + a_m * kq''^T (compute both directly)\ndef p1_logits_v2():\n    qk = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\n    kq = k @ q.transpose(-1, -2)  # This is A''^T, same cost as A\n    return (a_p * qk + a_m * kq) * inv_sqrt_d\nbench(\"a_p*qk''^T + a_m*kq''^T (2 matmuls)\", p1_logits_v2)\n\n# Alternative: compute symmetrized directly\n# a_p * qk''^T + a_m * kq''^T = (a_p/2 + a_m/2)*(qk''^T + kq''^T) + (a_p/2 - a_m/2)*(qk''^T - kq''^T)\n# = 0.5*(qk''^T + kq''^T) + 0.5*alpha*(qk''^T - kq''^T) [since a_p+a_m=1, a_p-a_m=alpha]\n# Not sure if helpful.\n\n# What about: compute p1 logits without materializing full A?\n# For softmax we need the full matrix... so no.\n\nPYEOF\npython /tmp/profile8.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
